{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_271176d85b3c2c1ba12200881f379ef5bf997fab35cb498b21dda0744953b8da", "title": "Afterplay (play)", "text": "Afterplay is a 2002 one-act play by Brian Friel. It centres on two characters from Chekhov (Sonya from \"Uncle Vanya\" and Andrey from \"Three Sisters\") meeting in Moscow in the 1920s.", "score": 33.6014}, {"id": "hp_doc_627ac681373d9c52cf9c503235c58d718cd0324d195db44326a0cdfac9244507", "title": "Uncle Vanya (1970 film)", "text": "Uncle Vanya (Russian: Дядя Ваня , \"Dyadya Vanya \" ) is a 1970 film adaptation of the Anton Chekhov play of the same title and directed by Andrey Konchalovskiy.", "score": 10.3787}, {"id": "hp_doc_1c4d316a1abe2df06a50e46c4023969f37b423bff0902ffb506afd1da6d881e4", "title": "Uncle Vanya (1963 film)", "text": "Uncle Vanya is a 1963 British film adaptation of the work \"Uncle Vanya\" by Anton Chekhov. The film was directed by Stuart Burge. It was a filmed version of the Chichester Festival production, directed by (and starring) Laurence Olivier as Astrov, and also starring Michael Redgrave (Vanya), Rosemary Harris (Elena), and Joan Plowright (Sonya).", "score": 8.5924}], "remaining_searches": 2}
